          "guid": "mtp7o4ob9kk88jju",
          "message": {
            "text": "Studio file paths are resolved beneath one server-owned workspace before any read or write. The injected path API makes the same escape rule testable under POSIX and Windows semantics; the client never supplies or widens the workspace root. Saves then validate and replace through a sibling temporary file so an invalid or interrupted write cannot truncate the last valid project.",
            "markdown": "Studio file paths are resolved beneath one server-owned workspace before any read or write. The injected path API makes the same escape rule testable under POSIX and Windows semantics; the client never supplies or widens the workspace root. Saves then validate and replace through a sibling temporary file so an invalid or interrupted write cannot truncate the last valid project."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/studio/app-projects.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 33,
                  "endLine": 50,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/** Resolve a UI-supplied project path without letting it escape the workspace. */\nexport function resolveStudioWorkspacePath(\n  workspaceRoot: string,\n  requestedPath: string,\n  pathApi: StudioPathApi = nativePath,\n): string {\n  const requested = requestedPath.trim();\n  if (requested === \"\") throw new Error(\"project path is required\");\n  const root = pathApi.resolve(workspaceRoot);\n  const resolved = pathApi.resolve(root, requested);\n  const relative = pathApi.relative(root, resolved);\n  if (relative === \"..\" || relative.startsWith(`..${pathApi.sep}`) || pathApi.isAbsolute(relative)) {\n    throw new Error(`project path must stay inside the Studio workspace: ${root}`);\n  }\n  if (pathApi.extname(resolved).toLowerCase() !== \".json\") {\n    throw new Error(\"Studio project files must use a .json extension\");\n  }\n  return resolved;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
